What is the definition of whole body oxygen delivery, and how is it calculated?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The definition of whole-tissue oxygen delivery is $\boxed{\text{the total amount of oxygen delivered to all tissues in the body per unit time.}}$ It is calculated using Fick's equation:  
\[
\text{VO}_2 = \text{VO}_2 \times \text{O}_2 \text{ content}
\]  
where:  
- $\text{VO}_2$ is the volume of oxygen consumed per unit time (e.g., mL/min).  
- $\text{VO}_2 \times \text{O}_2 \text{ content}$ is the product of the volume of oxygenated plasma per unit time (VO$_2$) and the oxygen content of the plasma (O$_2$ content).  

This equation is derived from the principle that the amount of oxygen delivered to the tissues is equal to the amount of oxygen consumed by the tissues.
