   \[
   65 \text{ lb} \times \frac{1 \text{ kg}}{2.2 \text{ lb}} = 30.45 \text{ kg}
   \]

2. **Convert height to meters**:
   \[
   3 \text{ ft} \times 30.48 \text{ cm/ft} + 6 \text{ in} \times 2.54 \text{ cm/in} = 9.04 \text{ cm} + 15.16 \text{ cm} = 10.1 \text{ cm} = 1.01 \text{ m}
   \]

3. **Calculate the body surface area (BSA)** using the Duywer-Duywer formula:
   \[
   \text{BSA} = \sqrt{\frac{1.89 \times \text{mass (kg)} \times \text{height (m)}}}{100} = \sqrt{\frac{1.89 \times 30.45 \times 1.01}{100}} = 1.15 \text{ m}^2
   \]

4. **Determine the drug dose**:
   \[
   17.5 \text{ mg/m}^2 \times 1.15 \text{ m}^2 = 20.225 \text{ mg}
   \]

Thus, the drug should be administered in a dose of \(\boxed{20.225 \text{ mg}}\) daily.

