Retinoic acid signaling can influence the differentiation of CD4+ T cells into different subtypes, such as:

1. B cell-promoting: RA promotes the differentiation of CB4+ T cells into B cell-promoting B cell cells, which are essential for promoting B cell survival and proliferation. This is particularly important in the context of humotic response.

