2. Optimal ratio: Studies have shown that a ratio of 50:1 (TiO2:GO) or 70:1 (TiO2:GO) can provide the best trade-between between efficiency and stability. This ratio provides sufficient TiO2 to provide efficient charge transport while maintaining the optimal amount of GO to enhance the performance of the solar cell.

The ratio of TiO2 and GO affects the overall efficiency and stability of the solar cell in the following ways:

1. Efficiency: The addition of GO to the TiO2 nanoparticles can improve the efficiency of the solar cell by enhancing the light absorption, charge separation, and charge transport properties of the active layer. This is due to the unique electronic and structural properties of GO, which can facilitate the transfer of electrons from the dye to the TiO2 nanoparticles.

