2. **Diatomic gas (e.g., \( \text{O}_2, \text{N}_2 \)):**  
   - At low temperatures, \( C_v = \frac{5R}{2} \) (translational and rotational degrees of freedom).  
   - At high temperatures, vibrational degrees of freedom contribute, so \( C_v > \frac{5R}{2} \).  

Thus, the correct options are \(\boxed{b}\) and \(\boxed{d}\).
