   - The area of a polygon depends on its type (triangle, square, penillion, etc.).
   - For a polygon with 12 sides (dodecagon), the area is given by:
     \[
     \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times \text{Perimeter} \times \text{Appendicular Height}
