#### (iii) Time constant:  
\[
\tau = \frac{m c_p}{h A} = \frac{1.2 \times 385}{56.8 \times 0.075} = 10.5 \, \text{s}
\]  

#### (iv) Maximum convective heat transfer coefficient for lumped model:  
The lumped model is valid if the temperature gradient inside the material is negligible. This is valid if the thermal resistance of the material is much larger than the thermal resistance of the convective boundary. The ratio of these resistances is:  
\[
\frac{1}{h A} \gg \frac{L}{k A}
