<start_of_turn>model
","(a) The force on the proton is given by \(F = qE\), where \(q\) is the charge of the proton and \(E\) is the electric field strength.  
\[
F = (1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C}) \times (500 \, \text{N/C}) = 8.00 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}
\]
Using Newton's second law, \(F = ma\), the acceleration \(a\) is:
\[
a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{8.00 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} = 4.78 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2
\]
Thus, the magnitude of the acceleration is \(\boxed{4.78 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2}\).

(b) The time \(t\) the proton takes to reach a speed \(v = 35,000 \, \text{m/s}\) is given by:
\[
t = \frac{v}{a} = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s}}{4.78 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2} = 6.56 \times 10^{-8} \, \text{s}
\]
Thus, the time is \(\boxed{6.56 \times 10^{-8} \, \text{s}}\).
