","1. **Calculate the mass of the satellite**:  
   The gravitational force \( F = mg \), where \( m \) is the mass of the satellite and \( g \) is the acceleration due to gravity.  
   \[
   m = \frac{F}{g} = \frac{3600 \, \text{N}}{9 \, \text{m/s}^2} = 400 \, \text{kg}
   \]

2. **Calculate the kinetic energy**:  
   The kinetic energy \( KE \) is given by \( KE = \frac{1}{2} mv^2 \), where \( m \) is the mass and \( v \) is the velocity.  
   \[
   KE = \frac{1}{2} (400 \, \text{kg}) (800 \, \text{m/s})^2 = \frac{1}{2} (400 \, \text{kg}) (640000 \, \text{m}^2/\text{s}^2) = 1280000 \, \text{J} = 1.28 \times 10^6 \, \text{J}
   \]

   Therefore, the kinetic energy of the satellite is \(\boxed{1.28 \times 10^6 \, \text{J}}\).
