   \[
   R = \left(1 - \frac{1}{\eta}\right)^{-1/(\gamma - 1)} = \left(1 - \frac{1}{0.56}\right)^{-1/(1.4 - 1)} = 2.64
   \]

2. **Work Done (W)**:
   The work done in the Otto cycle is given by:
   \[
   W = \left(1 - \frac{1}{R^{\gamma - 1}}\right) \cdot q_{in}
   \]
   The heat rejected (\(q_{\text{out}}\)) is given as 544 kJ/kg. For the Otto cycle, the heat added (\(q_{in}\)) is:
   \[
   q_{in} = q_{out} + W
   \]
   Substituting \(q_{in}\) into the work equation:
   \[
   W = \left(1 - \frac{1}{R^{\gamma - 1}}\right) \cdot (q_{out} + W)
   \]
