   \]  

   The temperature difference \( \Delta T \) is:  
   \[
   \Delta T = 500°C - 100°C = 400°C
   \]  

   The rate of heat transfer \( Q \) is:  
   \[
   Q = h \cdot A \cdot \Delta T = 423 \times (0.2 \times 0.1) \times 400 = 33,840 \text{ W}
   \]  

