   - \( F_a = P_a A_p = 100 \times 10^3 \, \text{Pa} \times 0.006287 \, \text{m}^2 = 628.7 \, \text{N} \)

5. **Balancing the forces:**
   \[
   F_A = F_B + F_g + F_a
   \]
   \[
   3926.1 \, \text{N} = P_B \times 0.006287 \, \text{m}^2 + 245.175 \, \text{N} + 628.7 \, \text{N}
   \]
   \[
   P_B = \frac{3926.1 - 245.175 - 628.7}{0.006287} = 3926.1 - 245.175 - 628.7 = 3172.225 \, \text{N}
   \]
   \[
   P_B = \frac{3172.225}{0.006287} = 500,000 \, \text{Pa} = 500 \, \text{kPa}
   \]

Thus, the gas pressure in cylinder B is \(\boxed{500 \, \text{kPa}}\).
